# Images (screenshots, dumps)
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.ppm

# B1051 verify leg: the three-way oracle|x86|xu4 evidence stills and the
# pose-line log excerpts are deliverables (refactor/B1051/VERIFY.md), not
# debug dumps -- the H02 tests/goldens negation above is the same precedent.
!refactor/B1051/evidence/**/*.jpg
!refactor/B1051/evidence/**/*.log

# B1152 (#472): the two oracle-leg strips (refactor/B1152/TRACE.md sec. 8 cites
# them as committed evidence; strip_regen.py in the evidence directory
# regenerates them and re-runs the per-cell census).
!refactor/B1152/strips/*.png

# H02: golden-frame PNGs are intentionally committed (tests/goldens/manifest.json
# records what they were blessed under; scripts/ci/visual_gate.sh compares against them)
!tests/goldens/*.png

# B1058/B1059: the oracle driver's template library and glyph atlas are data the
# driver reads (manifest.tsv / atlas.tsv pin each PNG's sha256). B1058's 40
# templates were never committed under the *.png rule; B1059 restores them,
# regenerated from manifest.tsv (source + rect), every sha256 matching.
!scripts/eqemu/oracle/templates/*.png
!scripts/eqemu/oracle/glyphs/*/*.png

# B893 (#209): the raw oracle wirecaps behind the [MEASURED] arc apex
# (eqemu zone log; the review rule is a [measured] claim carries its capture)
!refactor/B893/evidence/*.log

# B1013 (#334): the GEM event-log fixture behind the pool-timeline column
# (the B997 shipped-default qeynos2 leg's bo_events.log; the test pins its sha256)
!tests/data/b1013/*.log

