# Runtime caches (the shader-binary cache lives outside the checkout, B959)
# T402 (board B248): the two generated archive indices. They used to be
# TRACKED here, so every client run left the working tree dirty and a careless
# `git add -A` committed one machine's absolute EQ path. They are caches (a
# miss costs a rescan) and the client now writes them to a run-local cache
# directory -- $WILLEQ_CACHE_DIR, $WILLEQ_DATA_ROOT/cache or <exe dir>/cache.
# These two lines cover a stale copy left in an existing checkout.
config/snd_index_cache.json
config/gfx_index_cache.json
/cache/

# Runtime data
data/detail/
data/region_maps/
data/eq_client
data/eqe1_client
data/captures

# Recorded sessions / packet captures for replay-oracle tests (Batch R).
# Never checked in: contains real server/account traffic. Golden replay
# snapshots generated alongside them are also local-only.

# Agent working directory
.agent/
third_party/irrlicht-gles2-x86/
# T118 Leg 2: 32-bit sibling of the above, built the same way (irrlicht-drm
# sources + irrlicht-drm-patch.py, `make CXX="g++ -m32" ... staticlib`) for
# an i386 ASAN tree. Same local-build-artifact status as the x86_64 one.
third_party/irrlicht-gles2-x86-m32/
build-gles2/

# Q01 (repo hygiene): benchmarks/pi_runs/ used to be gitignored here
# (H04-era), which is how P05's "committed" CSVs silently never landed
# (salvaged 3fb85fc, see refactor/deferred.md "Repo hygiene"). Unignored so
# unit deliverable CSVs can never silently vanish again -- commit each unit's
# artifacts explicitly; do not mass-add pre-existing untracked run dirs.

# SQLite transient sidecar files -- never commit these (see below)
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

# T493: per-lane client configs. `scripts/scenario_configs/*.json` ships the
# default lane (the eqemu VM); a lane whose server is somewhere else -- the
# local stack, say -- copies one to `<name>.local.json` and edits the host
# there. The shipped originals' "host" is never edited in place.
scripts/scenario_configs/*.local.json
!tests/goldens/pi/**/*.png
# B1044: the Mac golden set (blessed by Will 2026-10-19) lives beside the Pi set
!tests/goldens/mac/**/*.png

# B1208: `rbuild --via ci` downloads the CI job's artifacts here
.rbuild-ci/
.spike-downloads/
